{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ecs"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them in a declared order."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ECS is an entity component system for Swift. It suits any program that updates many similar","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"things each step, such as the bodies of a physics simulation or the characters of a game.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Entities are lightweight handles. An ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","isActive":true},{"text":" holds no data of its own.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Components are plain value types, such as a position or a velocity, attached to entities."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"},{"text":" holds the entities and their components, along with ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"resources"}]},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"values the world holds once, such as a clock.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems are rules that read and change the world through queries and updates, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","type":"reference"},{"text":" runs them in the order you write, at the same time where they don’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs a world frame by frame, with a fixed timestep and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"states."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A world is a copy-on-write value, like an array: copies are cheap and independent, so you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keep one for a snapshot, an undo step or a rollback.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example, using the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" components from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", spawns a ball and moves it one step by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import ECS","","var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"import ECS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation, and you can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"import one on its own.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule"],"title":"Modules","anchor":"Modules"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"ECS","modules":[{"name":"ECS"}],"symbolKind":"module","title":"ECS","roleHeading":"Framework"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"role":"symbol","title":"Schedule","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Entity":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/entity","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle that identifies one entity in a world."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Entity","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","title":"Entity","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"World","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule":{"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule","abstract":[{"text":"Run a world frame by frame, with schedules for startup, a fixed timestep and each frame, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with states that switch systems on and off.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule","role":"collection","title":"SimulationModule","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"Systems","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS":{"url":"\/documentation\/ecs","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Build games and simulations from entities, the components they hold, and systems that update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them in a declared order."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS","role":"collection","title":"ECS","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://SimulationModule/documentation/SimulationModule/Simulation":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A world and its schedules by label, advanced one frame at a time.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"Simulation","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SimulationModule\/documentation\/SimulationModule\/Simulation","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Simulation","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/simulationmodule\/simulation"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries, updates, and commands."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"WorldModule","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule"},"doc://ECS/documentation/ECS/GettingStarted":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Define components, spawn entities, and move them with systems that run in a schedule and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simulation."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ECS\/documentation\/ECS\/GettingStarted","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/ecs\/gettingstarted","title":"Getting Started with ECS","kind":"article"}}}